<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hui Shung to tender 108,000T U.S. soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hui Shung to tender 108,000T U.S. soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp will tender on Wednesday for two combined shipments, consisting of 38,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans and 16,000 tonnes of U.S. No. 2 corn, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The Hui Shung Group includes Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp, Eagle Food Industry and Charoen Pokphand.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>    One	16,000   corn    U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>    One	38,000   soy     Jan 5-20   Jan 21- Feb 4</p>
<p>    Two	16,000   corn    U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>    Two	38,000   soy     Feb 5-20   Feb 21- Mar 7</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
